"**Header:**\n\u2022 Patient: Alex  \n\u2022 Encounter type: Telehealth consult  \n\n**S - Subjective:**\n\u2022 CC: 4 days feeling \u201cunder the weather\u201d  \n\u2022 HPI:\n  \u2022 Onset after close contact with sneezing colleague (suspected viral exposure from colleague\u2019s children in kindergarten)  \n  \u2022 Initially sore throat + runny nose  \n  \u2022 Sore throat: painful swallowing for 1\u20132 days, now improving; pt did not inspect throat; no noted white spots/redness  \n  \u2022 Nasal sx: started runny, now congested/\u201cstuffed,\u201d persistent nasal blockage  \n  \u2022 Cough: started yesterday, dry, constant through the day, not painful  \n  \u2022 Night sweats for several nights; makes pt tired/uneasy  \n  \u2022 Fever: present at beginning, now settling; relieved with paracetamol + ibuprofen  \n  \u2022 Dyspnea: \u201cwinded\u201d/more SOB on exertion, no SOB at rest; stopped going to gym; still managing to go to work  \n  \u2022 No chest pain  \n  \u2022 Fatigue, \u201cbad and tired\u201d  \n\u2022 ROS:\n  \u2022 ENT: No ear pain, no ear blockage, no ear discharge  \n  \u2022 Neuro: Headaches, generalized, intermittent; no visual disturbance; no photophobia  \n  \u2022 GI/GU: No nausea or vomiting; bowels OK; passing urine OK  \n  \u2022 Appetite: Eating slightly less than usual; drinking more than usual  \n  \u2022 Skin: No rashes  \n  \u2022 MSK: General muscle/joint aches over past couple of days  \n\u2022 PMH: Otherwise fit and well; no ongoing medical problems  \n\u2022 Meds: Paracetamol, ibuprofen (for fever)  \n\u2022 Allergies: No known drug allergies reported  \n\u2022 FH:\n  \u2022 Grandmother: DM, likely type 2  \n  \u2022 Great-grandfather: eczema  \n\u2022 SH:\n  \u2022 Lives alone  \n  \u2022 Occupation: Accountant; currently busy/stressful end-of-year period; slightly slower at work due to illness  \n  \u2022 Mood: Feels stress is \u201cgood kind,\u201d likes job; denies mood concerns  \n  \u2022 Smoking: Occasional cigars at company parties (not regular)  \n  \u2022 Alcohol: Occasional, social; \u201cnot a very big drinker\u201d  \n\n**O - Objective:**\n\u2022 Telehealth; no physical exam or vitals documented  \n\n**A - Assessment:**\n1. Viral upper respiratory tract infection / possible early influenza  \n   \u2022 4 days of sore throat (improving), nasal congestion, new dry cough, myalgias, intermittent headaches, initial fever now settling, night sweats, mild exertional SOB, preserved oral intake and hydration, systemically well enough to work  \n\n**P - Plan:**\n\u2022 Symptomatic management:\n  \u2022 Continue paracetamol and ibuprofen as needed per usual dosing  \n  \u2022 Rest; advised taking 1\u20132 days off work  \n  \u2022 Maintain good oral hydration (\u201cpush fluids\u201d)  \n\u2022 Safety-netting / follow-up:\n  \u2022 If not improving by next week, return for review  \n  \u2022 Seek earlier review/urgent care if: high or persistent fever, worsening or new chest pain, increasing or new SOB (esp. at rest), or if generally feeling significantly worse  \n\u2022 Education:\n  \u2022 Reassured likely self-limiting viral illness (URTI / early flu), typically resolves over ~7\u201310 days with gradual improvement"